AB  - In the last few years, Colombia has been improving its economic indicators. Today, the government believes that the country is attractive to domestic and foreign investment, especially in the agricultural sector and particularly in the oil palm industry, which the government has been promoting successfully. The following are, among others, good reasons to invest in Colombia: · Security: today, our law enforcement agencies are present in all Colombian municipalities, which has resulted in significantly lower rates of homicides, kidnappings, etc. · Macroeconomic stability: the growth rate of the Colombian economy in the last three years, including 2006, will be at about 4.6% annually. · Competitive interest rates · Access to credit instruments · Improved business climate · More investment in science and technology · Improved infrastructure · Institutional framework. Oil palm is one of the sectors with the strongest institutional framework in the Colombian agricultural sector.
